4.06
16/08/2026
Outlook Restart Required:,True
*** Test 6 of update ***
First release of the new VSTO-based EmailSync add-in.
Full rewrite of the sync engine, duplicate handling, and folder
management, migrated from the original VBA version. Debug logging
and error reporting have also been substantially improved.
EOF
EmailSyncSetup.msi,https://github.com/EmailSync-au/EmailSync-Distribution/releases/download/v4.06/EmailSyncSetup.msi
EOF



Developer notes for update settings (new VSTO / GitHub format):
Line 1: Version number (e.g. "4.0") — parsed as Double, must be a valid number
Line 2: Version date (informational only, not parsed for logic)
Line 3: Outlook Restart Required:,True or False
         True whenever the add-in DLL itself is being replaced (i.e. almost
         every real release) — the DLL is locked in memory while Outlook
         runs, so it can only be replaced via the MSI + Outlook restart path.
         False is only valid for a soft update shipping a standalone file
         that Outlook does NOT hold a lock on (e.g. UserGuide.pdf on its own).
Line 4..n: What's New notes — free text, shown verbatim in the update prompt
Line n: EOF
Line n+1: [FileName],[https://github.com/... direct download URL]
           — for a hard update (reboot=True): exactly one entry, the .msi
             release asset (release-download URL, NOT raw.githubusercontent).
           — for a soft update (reboot=False): one or more entries, individual
             files such as UserGuide.pdf. Destination directory is no longer
             specified here — ResolveSoftUpdateDestination() in
             UpdateChecker.vb decides it based on the file name.
Line n+i+1: EOF

Note: StopWords.txt is NOT listed here. It is checked and self-healed
independently at every Outlook startup (SyncEngine.StartUp), regardless of
software version — see the "Required file" step there, not this manifest.
